+2026-08-03 feat/367-landing-page — §10 escalation (rule extension). ONE question, raised by the
+build gate rather than by a reviewer, and it blocks the landing page from building.
+
+  THE FACTS. `site_v2/src/specs/page-spec.schema.json` makes `mart` a REQUIRED field on every
+  block, and `check-page-specs.mjs:259` refuses any value that is not a real file under
+  `dbt_project/models/5_marts/**`. Two of the landing page's four blocks are not mart-backed and
+  cannot be:
+    - Hybrid browse reads the COMPETITION REGISTRY (`build_nav` over
+      `docs/competition_registry.yml`). That is deliberate architecture, not a gap: the zero-file
+      rule requires a new league to appear with a registry entry and no model. A "registry mart"
+      would duplicate a seed to satisfy a checker.
+    - The fixtures hero reads `core.fct_fixture`, the same upcoming-fixture filter
+      `fetch_fixture_payloads` already uses for the shipped fixture page. There is no mart of
+      upcoming fixtures: `mart_team_fixtures` is team-perspective and deliberately drops
+      `fixture_sk` (GAP-19), so it cannot produce a match URL.
+  Verified, not assumed: `mart` required in the schema's `blocks.items.required`; the file check at
+  check-page-specs.mjs:259; `_shape_team_fixture`'s drop set in scripts/export_site_data.py.
+
+  WHY IT IS THE CPO'S. Changing what the page-spec contract accepts is a rule extension and a
+  build-gate mechanism change (CLAUDE.md §10). The home page is the FIRST page whose blocks are not
+  all mart-backed, so this is not a defect in my spec, it is a case the contract has never had to
+  express.
+
+  PATH A — extend the contract to name a non-mart source explicitly, e.g. `registry:competitions`
+  and `core:fct_fixture`, with the checker validating those forms against the real registry file
+  and the real core model. The gate keeps its guarantee (everything declared exists) and gains the
+  vocabulary to describe a registry-backed block. Touches page-spec.schema.json,
+  check-page-specs.mjs and its test.
+
+  PATH B — leave the contract alone and make every block mart-backed. This does not actually close:
+  a fixtures mart is buildable, but a registry mart is not honest, because the registry is a seed
+  the zero-file rule deliberately keeps out of the model layer.
+
+  RECOMMENDATION: Path A. Path B cannot satisfy the browse block without duplicating the registry
+  into a model, which contradicts the rule the browse block exists to honour. Path A keeps the
+  gate's real guarantee — nothing is declared that does not exist — and stops it asserting
+  something that was never true, that every block comes from a mart.
